// Custom trader city: replaces DayZ-Expansion-Market's 6 stock Chernarus
// trader zones (Svetloyarsk, BalotaAircrafts, KamenkaBoats, GreenMountain,
// Kamenka, Krasnostav - self-generated by the mod into MISSION_DIR/
// expansion/traderzones/ on first world load, confirmed live - see
// MODS.md) with a single custom-designed one, per TODO.md's world-crafting
// checklist ("decide whether to keep/relocate/replace these zones... once
// custom traders are designed").
//
// Starting roster (deliberately small, per project decision): one general
// "Everything" trader plus one "Vehicle" trader, covering the essentials
// without needing to design/theme a dozen NPCs up front. Neither is one of
// DayZ-Expansion-Market's 17 default trader identities (Weapons, Clothing,
// Consumables, etc. under profiles/ExpansionMod/Traders/) - those ship
// untouched (see ensureCustomTraderIdentities()) for later use once more
// specific/themed traders are wanted; only these two custom identities are
// referenced by the actual NPCs below.
//
// This only defines the *shape* of the zone (radius/pricing) and its NPC
// roster. The actual world position is a one-time, hands-on decision this
// file deliberately refuses to guess at: scout a real spot in-game as admin
// (see MODS.md's "Admin tools" section - COT's free cam/`INSERT` plus its
// position readout, or `H` to teleport back to it), then fill in
// CUSTOM_POSITION below. Until that's set, this only removes the 6 defaults
// and leaves the custom zone/NPCs disabled (with a warning) rather than
// writing NPCs to a guessed, possibly-underground position.
//
// NPCs are placed via Expansion's plain-text `.map` format (one line each:
// `<TraderEntityClassName>.<TraderFileName>|<Position>|<Orientation>|<Gear>`)
// under MISSION_DIR/expansion/traders/ - confirmed directly from
// DayZ-Expansion-Core's own script source (unpacked ai_scripts/core_scripts
// PBOs; the wiki page describing this is gone from GitHub), specifically
// ExpansionWorldObjectsModule.c's GetTraderFromMissionFile()/ProcessGear().
// Individual NPC positions here are *offsets* from CUSTOM_POSITION (baked in
// at generation time), so only one real-world coordinate ever needs
// scouting.
//
// The Gear field is a comma-separated token list (NOT a filename by itself);
// the only token used here is `loadout:<Name>`, which applies a named gear
// preset from profiles/ExpansionMod/Loadouts/<Name>.json (written by
// ensureCustomTraderGear() below) via ExpansionHumanLoadout.Apply(). That
// preset file's schema (ExpansionPrefabObject/InventoryAttachments) is
// DayZ-Expansion-Core's own and is NOT the same as DayZ-Editor's exported
// character-preset JSON (attachmentSlotItemSets/discreteItemSets) - the
// latter had to be manually converted into the former (see TRADER_BLUE_GEAR).

